==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Quarterback Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Gridiron Cat''' when obtained from [[NEO Wanwan's Glory]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Stat-wise, he can be considered as a diet version of [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]. Compared to Housewife, his health, damage, and DPS are significantly lower, his attack area is smaller and his standing range is lower, but he attacks faster and much more frequently and recharges faster. Despite having a lower maximum effective range than Housewife, he is capable of reaching just as far into the enemy backline thanks to his lower standing range.

Instead of slowing and permanently killing [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]], he is strong against Dark enemies and immune to [[Wave Attack]]s. The former ability makes him slightly better against Dark enemies than Housewife Cat, assuming his lower range isn't a problem. The latter ability allows him to be used somewhat safely against wave enemies, though his speed could result in him charging into the enemy's attack range when they are knocked back and his low DPS (except against [[Two Can]]) combined with longer than necessary recharge time makes him a generally inferior choice compared to non-immune units like [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]].

All things considered, there is little reason to use him if the player can use Housewife Cat, a better [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark]], or a better [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|wave-immune unit]] instead, keyword being ''if''. Thanks to his rarity, he can be used in Level 4 [[Legend Stages#Crown Difficulty|Legend Stages]], which is one of his few viable uses due to his Long Distance and wave-immune capabilities there.

==='''True Form'''===
While Gridiron Cat's stat boosts are nice, they mainly exist to improve what Quarterback Cat already did, which wasn't much to begin with. However, he also targets [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies and is immune to [[Surge Attack|Surges]], an essential immunity for [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku units]]. While he does lack [[Shield Piercing]], his Strong Against ability makes his stats more acceptable, especially against Aku enemies, since they also have a knack for abusing Waves and Surges ([[Medu-san]], [[Wicked Face]], etc.). Despite these boosts, Gridiron's massive flaw in his low DPS (even against his own target traits) is not fixed at all and better units exist for {{4c}} Waves and Surges, such as [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] and Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon]]. If you have better anti-Wave and/or Surge options, use them over Gridiron.

