==Trivia==
*Rugby Cat's Japanese name, ''Nyamefuto'', is a portmanteau of ニャー ''nyā'' (the onomatopoeia for a cat's meow) and アメフト ''amefuto'' (American football).
*Gridiron Cat appears to be a reference to the [[wikia:hokuto:Outlaw|Outlaws]], the peons or "small fry" enemies from the manga and anime ''[[wikipedia:Fist of the North Star|Fist of the North Star]]''. His Japanese name, Nyachar (ニャッハー ''Nyahhā'') is very similar to "Hyachar" (ヒャッハー! ''Hyahhā!''), a catchphrase of Outlaws in the manga, and his mohawk and spiked shoulder pads are common elements of the Outlaws' designs, including [[wikia:hokuto:Outlaw (Hokuto Musou)|Outlaw]] from the game ''[[wikia:hokuto:Hokuto Musō|Hokuto Musō]]''. His Japanese description even mentions his [[wikia:hokuto:Tōki|Tōki]] (闘気, "Fighting Spirit").
**Gridiron Cat's design is also similar to [[wikia:saintseiya:Cassios|Cassios]] from ''[[wikipedia:Saint Seiya|Saint Seiya]]'', although Cassios doesn't have spikes on his shoulder pads.
*Prior to [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]], the "Hoho!" in Gridiron Cat's English description had quotation marks around it.

